WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
Organ donation. In one study,

2
00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:06.190
effective consent in
Germany was 12 per cent.

3
00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:10.250
In Austria, it was 99.98 per cent.

4
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:14.330
Two countries, the same yes-or-no
decision about donation,

5
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.310
yet results that could
hardly be further apart.

6
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.900
Could something as small
as the design of a form

7
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.190
really explain a gap like that?

8
00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:25.740
In this mission, you'll learn
the tools of choice architecture:

9
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.970
framing, defaults, and
restricted and mandated choice.

10
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:33.090
Then you'll weigh up nudges
against taxes and bans,

11
00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.450
and judge when each one makes sense.

12
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.550
Your mission: find out
how much a pre-ticked box

13
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.590
on a form can really change.
